  "notes": "USAGE:\n{過信|かしん} is used both as a noun and as a suru verb ({過信|かしん}する). The object of excessive trust is marked with を.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自分|じぶん}を{過信|かしん}する: to be overconfident in oneself\n- {技術|ぎじゅつ}を{過信|かしん}する: to place too much faith in technology\n- {過信|かしん}は{禁物|きんもつ}: overconfidence is dangerous\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{自信過剰|じしんかじょう} (overconfidence) specifically refers to excessive self-confidence, while {過信|かしん} can apply to excessive trust in anything — people, tools, experience, etc.",
